local-06 (budi, 2026-10-12): Marlin MoE repack without full-size temporaries.

vLLM 0.31.0 loads compressed-tensors MoE weights N-first and converts them in
_process_weights_marlin: it transposes w13 and w2 to contiguous K-first copies,
keeps both alive, then repacks. On top of the loaded weights a layer briefly
holds two full copies plus the repacked output. 0.30.0 loaded the weights
K-first and only needed the repack output. Qwen3.8-Flash-Next on 3 x 3090 fills
each card almost completely with weights, so the 0.31 build died at load:
torch.OutOfMemoryError in gptq_marlin_moe_repack (400 MiB, 5 MiB free) on PP0
and PP1.

This repacks 64 experts at a time (Marlin repacks each expert on its own, so
the result is unchanged) and, when an expert's repacked size equals its loaded
size, writes each chunk back over the loaded weights it was read from, so no
full-size output buffer is needed. Checked on an RTX 3060 with the model's MoE
shapes (512 experts, N 640, group 128): outputs identical to the one-shot path;
extra peak per layer 1980 MiB -> 192 MiB (a separate output buffer, rev 1:
1071 MiB, still OOMed the MTP build on PP1).
Drop once upstream stops materialising the transposed copies.

